   },
   "id": "2102555300691583043",
   "url": "https://x.com/DutchRojas/status/2102555300691583043",
   "conversationId": "2102555300691583043",
   "text": "I turn 51 today. Washington has spent 16 of those years restricting physicians from opening and expanding hospitals.\n\nAfter more than 25 years building healthcare businesses, here’s my birthday wish list:\n\n1. HHS, CMS, and Congress: end Medicare’s hospital markup. Why the hell are taxpayers paying hospitals more for the same procedures independent surgery centers already perform?\n\n2. Ban Certificate of Need laws nationwide. Repeal Section 6001’s restrictions on physician-owned hospitals. Stop choking off competition and acting shocked at the prices.\n\n3. Require prices patients and employers can compare before treatment and enforce when the bill arrives.\n\n4. Reform the 340B drug discount program. Show what hospitals pay, what they collect, and what patients receive in financial assistance. Tie the benefit to documented help for patients.\n\nDemocrats and Republicans have fundraisers. I have a birthday wish list.\n\nSomehow, their guests always get their wishes granted.\n\nP.S. Thanks to my Mom for the awesome Ai bday card.",
   "lang": "en",
   "createdAt": "2026-09-23T00:27:01.000Z",
